"""opos-updater: the root-side trust anchor of OPOS over-the-air updates (contract: docs/ota-update.md).

Standard library only. Subcommands: apply-inbox, apply-pending-boot, confirm-boot, rollback, status.

Every directory, command and limit comes from a Config. The CLI builds the production Config (fixed paths and
absolute command paths; no environment variable, argument or file overrides it); tests build temporary ones with
stubbed commands. Nothing here runs at import time.

Crash safety: before the first live change (overlay files, the /opt/opos symlink) state.json gets a `txn` record
and the old files are saved in the new release's overlay-backup/. Whatever stops the run after that (exception,
kill, power loss), the next run finds the record and puts the old release back (an apply is undone; an
interrupted rollback is finished). A release only becomes `current` after its health check passed. The updater
never restarts opos.service (the compositor session); the only unit it restarts is opos-server.service.
"""
